{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":2232929,"ns":0,"title":"Chronotope","extract":"In literary theory and philosophy of language, the chronotope is how configurations of time and space are represented in language and discourse. The term was taken up by Russian literary scholar Mikhail Bakhtin who used it as a central element in his theory of meaning in language and literature.","description":"Concept in literary theory","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}